@startsalt
' Screen: Expectation Editor (inline form on node detail pane)
' User Stories:
'   - As a tester, I can define a labeled expectation with a weight and direction
'   - As a tester, I can choose a scoring method for the expectation
'   - As a tester, when I select "rubric" scoring, a rubric picker appears
'   - As a tester, I can save or cancel editing an expectation

{
  == Edit Expectation ==
  ..
  {
    <b>Label</b> <color:red>*</color>
    "mentions_return_policy                    "
  }
  ..
  {
    <b>Weight</b> <i>(0.0 – 1.0)</i>   |   <b>Direction</b>
    "0.35                  "            |   (X) positive  () negative
  }
  ..
  {
    <b>Scoring Method</b>
    ^lm_judge ▼^
    ..
    <i>Options: lm_judge · rubric · regex · semantic · structural</i>
  }
  ..
  ' ── Conditional: shown when method = rubric ──────────────────────────
  {+
    <b>Rubric</b> <color:red>*</color>  <i>(required when scoring = rubric)</i>
    ^Select rubric... ▼^
    ..
    {#
      <b>Available Rubrics</b>      | <b>Version</b>
      hallucination-check    | v2
      policy-compliance      | v1
      tone-professional      | v3
    }
  }
  ==
  {
    [ Cancel ]  |  [ Save Expectation ]
  }
}

@endsalt
